# English-first naming

Use **English** as the default for all technical names in this repo.

## Must be English

- URL routes and path segments (`/login`, `/signup`, `/account`, `/activities`)
- React route `path` values and `Navigate`/`Link`/`NavLink` `to` targets
- File and folder names (`LoginPage.jsx`, `AccountPage.jsx`)
- Components, hooks, functions, variables, and constants
- API endpoints and query/body field names exposed by the backend
- Database table/column names when we control them (already `profiles`, `full_name`, etc.)
- Git branch names and commit message subjects when creating new ones
- Env var names (`VITE_SUPABASE_URL`, not Portuguese equivalents)

## May stay in Portuguese (or later i18n)

- User-visible copy in the UI (labels, buttons, errors shown to end users)
- Marketing / README prose aimed at Brazilian readers

## Examples

```text
✅ /login  /signup  /account  /activities
❌ /entrar  /cadastro  /conta  /atividades
```

When renaming a public route, add a temporary redirect from the old path if users might have bookmarked it.
